// WQL — A USER-AGGREGATE ARGUMENT IS CHECKED BY THE HOST COMPILER, AND THE
// DIAGNOSTIC NAMES A GENERATED LINE. THIS FILE PINS THAT, ON PURPOSE.
//
// `compute_agg_bodies` exempts a UDA's argument from `check_agg_operand`: the
// value is not emitted into an EL accumulator at all, it is printed into the
// user's `X_step`, whose declared T is the contract. But NOTHING READS THAT T.
// `resolve_aggs` checks `fn_param_count(d_step) != 2` and never asks
// `_step`'s param-1 TYPE, so the only thing that ever compares the column to the
// step's parameter is the host compiler, reporting from inside a metaprog blob.
//
// MEASURED at 0fb56500 on exactly this program, verbatim:
//   logosc rc = 1
//   <metaprog-blob-subst>:3922: error [fn q_run]: call to 'myag_step' arg 2:
//     expected i64, got f32
//   no object file
//
// ⚠ THIS IS A BAD DIAGNOSTIC, NOT A SOUNDNESS OR EXIT-CODE DEFECT, and the
// distinction is the reason this is a pin and not a fix. The mandate grouped it
// with `avg(str)`, which compiled rc=0 and WROTE AN OBJECT FILE; the measurement
// separates them. Nothing unsound compiles here. What is wrong is that the
// message names `<metaprog-blob-subst>:3922` and `myag_step`'s parameter instead
// of the `aggregate` clause, the aggregate and the column type — the same
// anti-pattern `check_agg_operand` was written to replace at the builtin sites.
//
// ⚠ AND CLOSING IT IS A RULING, NOT A REFACTOR. It needs a reflected
// `fn_param_type_name(view, decl, idx)` (~12 lines, mirroring `fn_param_count`
// in reflect.logos) plus routing `_step`'s declared param-1 type into
// `check_agg_operand` as `want`. That makes the wql handler the gatekeeper where
// the host compiler is the documented oracle today, and it can refuse programs
// that compile NOW — a `_step` taking `u8` against an `i8` column, say, which
// the host accepts by implicit widening and `el_host_carries` does not. The
// mitigation (apply the check only when `_step`'s T is IN the EL lattice, host
// as oracle otherwise) is a choice about what the language accepts, so it is
// Victor's.
//
// The assertion below deliberately omits the blob LINE NUMBER: the number moves
// with any change to the generated preamble, and pinning it would make this a
// test about the emitter's line count. When the diagnostic is fixed, this file's
// expectation is replaced by the clause-naming one — the pin is what makes that
// replacement a decision rather than a discovery.
package test;

use logos.std.wql.wql;
use logos.mem.collections.vec;

struct Rec { pub k: i64, pub v: f32 }

fn myag_init() -> i64 { return 0i64; }
fn myag_step(acc: i64, x: i64) -> i64 { return acc + x; }

pub deem q(src: &[Rec]) { from src s
      group by s.k
      aggregate m = myag(s.v)
      select m : i64 }

fn main() -> i32 { return 0i32; }
